      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have some reservations about including “maven” in this central module name, given how frequently it’s used across the codebase:\n\n```bash\n$ git grep gerrit-maven | wc -l\n193\n```\n\nPublishing to the Central Repository is a build-tool-agnostic task and could be done with different systems (e.g. Bazel, Buck2, Gradle). Because of that, it might make sense to choose a more neutral name.\n\nHow about renaming it to `gerrit-deps`? This would avoid any Maven-specific connotations while still conveying the purpose of the module.\n\nI just checked and noticed that in `jgit` it’s also called `jgit_deps`. We could call it `gerrit_deps`; personally, I’d prefer using a dash rather than an underscore in Bazel context.",
