      "writtenOn": "2026-01-08T17:00:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While testing this change, I’m seeing these rather noisy warnings when downloading sources:\n\n```bash\nWARNING: Download from https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com/com/google/auto/value/auto-value/1.11.0/auto-value-1.11.0-sources.jar failed: class java.io.FileNotFoundException GET returned 404 Not Found\nWARNING: Download from https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com/com/google/auto/value/auto-value/1.11.0/auto-value-1.11.0.jar failed: class java.io.FileNotFoundException GET returned 404 Not Found\nWARNING: Download from https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com/org/apache/pdfbox/xmpbox/2.0.24/xmpbox-2.0.24.jar failed: class java.io.FileNotFoundException GET returned 404 Not Found\n```\n\nIs this a known issue in RJE? Is there a way to avoid it?\nWe are specifying multiple repositories, and these artifacts (especially sources) are only available from Maven Central.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "fa010c8e61d204674b13beb36bf9b5679d9d59e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b073794e_59363260",
        "filename": "MODULE.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 43
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-08T22:00:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Google Maven Storage bucket (https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com) appears to host only two kinds of artifacts:\n\n* the Prolog compiler and runtime\n* the Gitiles servlet and Gitiles blame-cache\n\nSee:\n\n```python\ntools/deps.bzl:PROLOG_REPO \u003d GERRIT\ntools/deps.bzl:GITILES_REPO \u003d GERRIT\n```\n\nIt might be possible (not tested yet) to temporarily extract these artifacts into a dedicated dependency module, for example `google-deps`.\n\nFor instance:\n\n```python\nmaven.install(\n    name \u003d \"google-deps\",\n    repositories \u003d [\n        \"https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com\",\n    ],\n    ...\n)\n```\n\nand then define a dedicated TOML file for this module:\n\n```python\nmaven.from_toml(\n    name \u003d \"google-deps\",\n    libs_versions_toml \u003d \"//tools:google-deps.toml\",\n)\n```\n\nWith this approach, we could potentially remove the Google Storage bucket from line 58 above and avoid the related warnings.",
      "parentUuid": "929736e1_97679f85",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "fa010c8e61d204674b13beb36bf9b5679d9d59e3",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91c82050_1a0cb5f9",
        "filename": "MODULE.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 43
